{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":17,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" calculus students (+ college success future) (+ motivated inspired encouraged))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"jaime escalante\" calculus students (+ college success future) (+ motivated inspired encouraged))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_638824153#6_1349660670","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2135","rank":1,"snippet":"life \" , \"segment\": \"Just a couple of year later in 1982 eighteen of Escalante’s students passed the Advanced Placement Calculus exam. The results seemed faked, and therefore several students had to re-do the review, and twelve of the students who agreed to do the exam again, passed it. The number of students successfully passing the exam kept doubling from year to year, and Escalante got nationwide attention. In 1983 Jaime Escalante was invited to teach a <cover>Calculus class at East Los Angeles College. Recognition The success of Jaime Escalante was recognized and was real. His methods worked, and the number of students passing the exam was increasing which inspired </cover>a book and a movie to be produced. The book written by Jay Mathews was released in 1988 and was called “Escalante: The Best Teacher in America,” and a movie “Stand and Deliver” followed shortly. Further work After Escalante’s work became publicly known, he continued working and preparing students for the calculus exam. Some people disliked his popularity, and Jaime Escalante began receiving threat mail.\" , \"start_char\": 3047.000000 , \"title\": \"Jaime "},"time":102},"model_calls":17,"document_judgments":11,"relevance_3":3,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
