{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":70,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"stand and deliver\" escalante students (+ \"college\" \"career\" \"careers\" \"future\") (+ math calculus))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"stand and deliver\" escalante students (+ \"college\" \"career\" \"careers\" \"future\") (+ math calculus))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2181","rank":1,"snippet":"didn't dampen the enthusiasm of many Garfield graduates, who came from all over Los Angeles and beyond to show their support for their former teacher, Jaime Escalante. Escalante's former students recently learned he is in the end stages of bladder cancer that has spread throughout his body. The medical costs have depleted Escalante's savings, and the students are determined to help out. 'Barrio Kids' To the astonishment of the outside world, Escalante taught many of these returning graduates math — advanced math, like trigonometry and calculus. Garfield educates some of Los Angeles' poorest students, many of them from immigrant families, and many of whom never conceived of <cover>college as a possibility. But Escalante did. Web Resources YouTube: Jaime Escalante On Being A Teacher YouTube: Actor Edward James Olmos As Jaime Escalante in \"Stand And Deliver\" The Bolivian-born teacher believed math was the portal to any success his students </cover>could achieve later in life.\" , \"start_char\": 6046.000000 , \"title\": \"Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies : NPR\" , \"url\": \"https://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=125380015\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":184},"model_calls":70,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":70,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"model_calls":70,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":70,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_675151580#14_1525686343","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2181","rank":2,"snippet":"000000 , \"headings\": \"What is “Brain-Based Learning”? What is “Brain-Based Learning”?\" , \"segment\": \"The regular, active processing of experience as the basis for making meaning. (Caine and Caine 1997) Real-life Examples Rather than offering a list of “how to’s,” Caine and Caine provide many illustrations of how these three elements may manifest themselves in real-life learning situations. They analyze, for instance, the success of famous math teacher Jaime Escalante, whose <cover>students from the Los Angeles barrio passed the calculus advanced placement exam in astounding numbers. They claim that Escalante, whose teaching career was portrayed in the movie “Stand and Deliver,” </cover>was using brain-based practices: “ Although we question his textbook approach to the content of the subject, he understands his students and the world students live in. In his classes, calculus becomes a way of life, is a source of pride, and is linked to deeper understanding of how mathematics opens doors to further study and the individual student’s future.” As the term “orchestrated immersion” implies, the teacher becomes the orchestrator, or the architect, designing experiences that will lead students to make meaningful connections. ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#14_1878661556","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":9},"model_calls":70,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
