{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":71,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#0_824515965","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2181","rank":4,"snippet":"transformative power of an effective teacher is something almost all of us have experienced and understand on a personal level. If we were particularly fortunate, we had numerous exceptional teachers who made school an exciting and interesting place. Those teachers possessed a passion for the subjects that they taught and genuine care for the students with whom they worked. They inspired us to play with ideas, think deeply about the subject matter, take on more challenging work, and even pursue <cover>careers in a particular field of study. Some exceptional teachers achieve celebrity status, such as Jaime Escalante, the math teacher who inspired the film Stand and Deliver, but thousands of unsung heroes go unrecognized in their remarkable work with students </cover>on a daily basis. Qualities of Effective Teachers We know intuitively that these highly effective teachers can have an enriching effect on the daily lives of children and their lifelong educational and career aspirations.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"The Power of an Effective Teacher and Why We Should Assess It\" , \"url\": \"http://www.ascd.org/publications/books/104136/chapters/The-Power-","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#0_824515965","rank":4,"relevance":1}]},"time":6},"model_calls":71,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
