{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":71,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#7_1878652119","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2181","rank":5,"snippet":"3908.000000 , \"headings\": \"Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies Obituaries Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies Students 'Stand And Deliver' For Former Teacher 'Barrio Kids' Web Resources After-Hours Tutoring Giving Back To 'Kimo' Fund public radio's future \" , \"segment\": \"In this scene, Escalante shows up at a family restaurant owned by the parents of one of his brightest <cover>students, Ana. Her father had pulled her out of Escalante's calculus class so that she could work more hours at the restaurant. Escalante tries to change his mind. (SOUNDBITE OF MOVIE, \"STAND AND DELIVER\") JAMES OLMOS: ( as Jaime Escalante) Ana can be the first one in your family to graduate from high school, go to college. </cover>JAMES VICTOR: ( as Mr. Delgado) Thank you for your concern. Her mother works here, her sisters, her brothers. This is a family business. She's needed.\" , \"start_char\": 3332.000000 , \"title\": \"Teacher Portrayed in 'Stand And Deliver' Dies : NPR\" , \"url\": \"https://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=125380015\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#7_1878652119","rank":5,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":71,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":71,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"model_calls":71,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":71,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2181"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_675151580#13_1525684520","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2181","rank":6,"snippet":"learning to occur: “ relaxed alertness,” “orchestrated immersion,” and “active processing.” An optimal state of mind that we call relaxed alertness, consisting of low threat and high challenge. The orchestrated immersion of the learner in multiple, complex, authentic experience. The regular, active processing of experience as the basis for making meaning. (Caine and Caine 1997) Real-life Examples Rather than offering a list of “how to’s,” Caine and Caine provide many illustrations of how these three elements may manifest themselves in real-life learning situations. They analyze, for instance, the success of famous math teacher Jaime Escalante, whose <cover>students from the Los Angeles barrio passed the calculus advanced placement exam in astounding numbers. They claim that Escalante, whose teaching career was portrayed in the movie “Stand and Deliver,” </cover>was using brain-based practices: “ Although we question his textbook approach to the content of the subject, he understands his students and the world students live in.\" , \"start_char\": 7182.000000 , \"title\": \"What is \\\"Brain-Based Learning\\\"? - Brain Connection\" , \"url\": \"https://brainconnection.brainhq.com/2004/03/26/what-is-brain-based-learning/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#1_824518445","rank":3,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_345449932#0_824515965","rank":4,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1039848851#7_1878652119","rank":5,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":71,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
