{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35620","model_call":87,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2193"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2193"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1127365340#8_2542320554","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2193","rank":3,"snippet":"Are you ready to discover your college program? 1. Build Mad Skills 2. Become Best Buds With Your Professor 3. Win Friends and Influence Classmates 4. Take a Crash Course 5. Earn Personal Gratification 6. Play To the Crowd 7. Get a Shot at the Big Leagues 8. Get Together (Come On People Now...) 9. Attain Wisdom It Takes Ganas: Jaime Escalante's Secret to Inspired Learning It Takes <cover>Ganas: Jaime Escalante''s Secret to Inspired Learning \" , \"segment\": \"3. Win Friends and Influence Classmates Being a TA isn't a popularity contest. On the other hand, it's nice to be liked. As a TA, you will have the opportunity to meet and directly interact with so many more of your fellow students. College </cover>campuses are often big, diverse places brimming with opportunities for engagement, but it doesn't mean you'll always know where to look. As a TA, you'll have an inbuilt opportunity to meet, befriend, and collaborate with your fellow students. Remember, you will likely only preside over a class of students for one semester. After that, you'll just be classmates again. As a TA, you'll get to ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1127365340#8_2542320554","rank":3,"relevance":0}]},"time":16},"model_calls":87,"document_judgments":49,"relevance_3":11,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
